REQ-PB-091 SOURCE DG5 | Implement the 25-question Transformation Health Check with score and top 3 actions 
   PROC: Assessor answers all 25 questions; score out of 25 is calculated; three top actions are required; reassessments tracked 
   ACC: A16: all 25 questions render verbatim; an assessment with an unanswered question is labelled incomplete and shows no band; submission without three actions is rejected 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0149, B0150, B0161): the 25 questions (checkboxes), 'Score: __ / 25' and 'Top 3 actions'. Master-prompt additions (§14 M0262, M0288): Yes=1/No=0 scoring (REQ-S14-001) and incomplete-assessment handling (REQ-S14-002), both implementation assumption D-010 (M0262); the top three improvement actions are required and reassessments are tracked over time (M0288). Interpretations: the requirement for three actions is enforced by rejecting submission of an assessment with fewer than three.

REQ-PB-092 SOURCE DG5 | Interpret the health-check score with the four source bands 
   PROC: Completed assessments show the band text matching the score 
   ACC: A16: scores 21, 16, 10 and 9 map to the four band texts verbatim 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0151, B0152): the four score bands and their text. Master-prompt additions: none; §14 M0288 restates the four bands (its top-three-actions and reassessment clause is covered by REQ-PB-091). Interpretations: none.

REQ-PB-001 SOURCE DG5 | Label the methodology provenance honestly as a practical synthesis inspired by PMI/Brightline/BRM and never claim official PMI status 
   PROC: System displays the verbatim provenance statement in the Playbook reader, About page and generated report footers; the source-foundations table (Source / Used for) is shown read-only in the Playbook reader 
   ACC: A01: provenance text on reader/About/report footer matches B0004 verbatim; an automated text scan of UI strings (en+ar) and report templates finds no claim of 'official PMI standard', 'PMI certified' or equivalent 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0004, B0024, B0155, B0156): the provenance statement and the source-foundations table (Source / Used for). Master-prompt additions (§2): showing the statement in the reader, the About page and report footers, and the automated scan for claims of official PMI status or certification. Interpretations: none beyond where the statement is displayed. The Arabic rendering of the statement needs linguistic review.

REQ-PB-002 SOURCE DG5 | Mark custom extensions of the playbook distinctly from PMI/Brightline-derived foundations 
   PROC: Each seeded methodology element (phases, TOM dimensions, gates, templates, scoring model, cadence, launch plan, health check, roaming example, traceability chain) carries a provenance attribute 'custom extension (playbook v1.0)' shown as a badge in the Playbook reader and Studio 
   ACC: A01: every seeded element listed in B0158-B0162 returns provenance=custom-extension from the API and renders the badge in en and ar; no such element is labelled as a PMI standard 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0154, B0157-B0162): the list of custom extensions. Master-prompt additions: none; §2 M0089 restates the practical-synthesis distinction, and the provenance badge is how the platform displays the source list. Interpretations: B0160 says 'most practical templates', so the platform tags all of T01-T16 as custom extensions unless an admin records otherwise.

REQ-PB-009 SOURCE DG4 | Apply 'Benefits before closure': an initiative is complete only when value is realized and sustained, not when delivered 
   PROC: Initiatives carry separate delivery, value-realization and sustainment statuses; closure requires validated benefits and sustainment owner or a documented transition decision 
   ACC: A11: an initiative with delivery=Complete and no validated benefit cannot be closed (API 409); UI shows 'Delivered — value validation pending' 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0014): the principle 'Benefits before closure'. Master-prompt additions (§3 M0092, §11 M0218): separate delivery, value-realization and sustainment statuses, and the documented transition decision. Interpretations: the closure rule (validated benefits plus a sustainment owner, or a transition decision), enforced as API 409.

REQ-PB-074 SOURCE DG4 | Implement the six-step benefits lifecycle Identify, Plan, Enable, Measure, Correct, Sustain 
   PROC: Each benefit progresses through the steps with the source output required per step 
   ACC: A04;A10;A11: a benefit cannot enter Measure without the Plan outputs; Sustain requires a BAU owner and control cadence 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0120, B0121): the six steps with their question and output. Master-prompt additions (§12 M0234): submitted benefit evidence is routed to the Finance queue. Interpretations: each step's outputs are preconditions (Measure needs the Plan outputs; Sustain needs a BAU owner and control cadence).

REQ-PB-077 SOURCE DG5 | Label the Realize phase as aligned with PMI BRM logic without claiming PMI standard status 
   PROC: The Realize phase guidance shows the note that it aligns with PMI Benefits Realization Management logic 
   ACC: A01: Realize guidance shows 'aligns with PMI Benefits Realization Management logic' and no 'certified'/'official' wording 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0124): the Realize phase aligns with PMI Benefits Realization Management logic. Master-prompt additions (§2 M0089): no 'certified' or 'official' wording. Interpretations: none. This is a labelling requirement.

REQ-PB-054 SOURCE DG3 | Support a transformation-level business case with lighter linked initiative cases 
   PROC: Initiative cases are lighter forms linked to the transformation case; roll-up references, not copies 
   ACC: A01;A10: an initiative case links to one transformation case; editing the initiative case changes the transformation roll-up without duplicating benefits 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0084): a transformation-level case, with lighter initiative cases underneath. Master-prompt additions (§8 M0173): the roll-up works by reference and never duplicates benefits. Interpretations: none.

REQ-PB-055 SOURCE DG3 | Require Finance validation of baseline and benefit logic early, before G4, not after delivery 
   PROC: A business case cannot be submitted as G4 evidence until Finance has validated its baseline and benefit formulas 
   ACC: A08;A10: G4 submission with a business case whose benefit formula is unvalidated is rejected listing 'Finance validation' 
   NOTES: Playbook (B0084, B0139): Finance should validate the baseline and benefit logic 'early—not after delivery', and be aligned on baselines and benefit formulas by day 90. Master-prompt additions: none. Interpretations: 'early' becomes a hard rule: a business case cannot serve as G4 evidence until Finance has validated its baseline and benefit formulas (AN-05 relabelling, finding F-DG0-003).

REQ-PB-058 SOURCE DG4 | Prevent double counting: each benefit has a unique owner, baseline, formula and financial-statement or non-financial KPI link 
   PROC: System rejects a benefit without a single owner, baseline, formula and a financial statement line or agreed non-financial KPI; initiatives link to canonical benefits via allocations, parent/child relationships and shared-benefit groups; portfolio totals sum canonical benefits, not links, so a shared benefit rolls up once 
   ACC: A10: a benefit with two owners is rejected; a 10 million SAR benefit shared by two initiatives appears once (10 million SAR) in the portfolio total 
   NOTES: Shared-benefit allocation rules detailed in master prompt §8. AN-04 consolidation: absorbs former REQ-S08-012 (Prevent double counting through a canonical benefit register, parent/child relationships, shared-benefit groups and contribution allocations so portfolio aggregation counts a shared benefit once); its anchors M0173 and acceptance are carried here. The canonical benefit register, parent/child relationships, shared-benefit groups and contribution allocations are the master prompt §8 mecha

