REQ-S07-007 USER DG4 M0160 | Compute RAG from the approved expected trajectory with configurable thresholds and never from project task completion 
   PROC: RAG = evaluation of actual versus expected-to-date by polarity using configured thresholds; task completion is not an input 
   ACC: A04;A05: with all tasks complete and actual below the red threshold the KPI is Red; changing the threshold version recomputes RAG

REQ-S01-005 ENGINEERING DG6 M0080 | Never imply an external operational change happened because a task was marked complete; require verified evidence or a confirmed integration result 
   PROC: Deliverables flagged as external changes carry a separate confirmation state that only reviewed evidence or a confirmed connector result can set; task completion alone leaves it Unconfirmed 
   ACC: A11;A17: marking the task complete leaves the deliverable Unconfirmed; a filename-only link does not confirm it; reviewed evidence or a test-adapter confirmation sets it and records the source

REQ-S03-002 USER DG4 M0092 | Let performance areas and BAU ownership continue indefinitely while transformations remain time-bounded 
   PROC: Closing a transformation does not close its performance areas; their KPIs, owners and review cadence remain active 
   ACC: A11: after a transformation is closed its linked performance area still generates scheduled review tasks and accepts KPI actuals

REQ-S03-003 USER DG4 M0092 | Keep initiative delivery, business adoption, validated value and transformation closure as separate statuses 
   PROC: Each status has its own state machine and owner; none is derived from another; views show all four side by side 
   ACC: A11: setting delivery to Complete leaves adoption, validated value and closure unchanged; the API rejects a closure request while validated value is pending unless a transition decision exists

REQ-S08-001 USER DG4 M0166 | Track planned, forecast, measured, submitted-for-validation, validated, rejected and sustained benefit values separately 
   PROC: Each benefit keeps separate value series per state; aggregations never combine states 
   ACC: A10: a forecast amount never appears in the validated total; a rejected measurement is retained and shown as rejected

REQ-S08-003 USER DG4 M0167 | Record for each benefit a unique ID, type, accountable business owner, Finance validator where applicable, baseline/counterfactual, formula, driver units, target, timing, one-off/recurring classification, currency, measurement source, evidence, confidence, assumptions, contribution links and financial-statement mapping or agreed non-financial KPI 
   PROC: Benefit profile form with server-side validation of required fields 
   ACC: A10: a financial benefit without a financial-statement mapping, or a non-financial one without an agreed KPI, is rejected

REQ-S08-008 ENGINEERING DG4 M0171 | Require the same period and a validated comparison basis for the cost reduction example 
   PROC: Cost reduction = eligible volume x reduction in unit cost for the same period; evaluation requires a Finance-validated comparison basis 
   ACC: A05;A10: with an unvalidated comparison basis the result is labelled provisional and excluded from validated totals

REQ-S08-013 USER DG4 M0173 | Reject allocations over 100% and show any share below 100% as unallocated 
   PROC: The server sums allocations per benefit; above 100% is rejected; below 100% shows the remaining share as unallocated 
   ACC: A10: allocations 60% + 50% are rejected; 60% + 30% saves and shows 10% unallocated

REQ-S13-008 USER DG5 M0254 | Label provisional or unvalidated values clearly in reports and exports 
   PROC: Values not validated carry a 'provisional' label 
   ACC: A10;A15: a pending benefit value is labelled provisional in the PDF pack

REQ-S04-002 USER DG4 M0116 | Make gates explicit approval records tied to a versioned, immutable evidence snapshot, never inferred from task completion 
   PROC: Submitting a gate freezes the linked evidence record versions into a snapshot; approvers decide on that snapshot; completing all tasks never changes gate state 
   ACC: A07;A08: completing every phase task leaves the gate Draft; editing a record after submission does not change the snapshot content shown to approvers

REQ-S04-012 USER DG4 M0125;M0228 | Block gate submission when mandatory evidence is missing unless a specifically authorized exception is recorded 
   PROC: Gate readiness is evaluated live and the gate page lists missing mandatory evidence; on submit the server checks each mandatory evidence item; missing items are listed and submission is refused unless an authorized, unexpired exception covers the item 
   ACC: A08: the gate page lists missing items; submission with one missing mandatory item returns 422 listing it; with a valid exception it succeeds and the snapshot records the exception

REQ-S15-002 USER DG1 M0004;M0291;M0293;M0294;M0295;M0296;M0297;M0298;M0299 | Seed the provisional design tokens brand.primary #0078FF, brand.deep #003B73, surface.page #F5F8FC, surface.card #FFFFFF, text.primary #142438, text.secondary #526174 and border.default #DCE5EF, labelled provisional and not official Mobily colours 
   PROC: Tokens are stored as configuration and applied through CSS variables; Branding Settings shows each token's provenance as 'provisional' until an admin loads official values 
   ACC: A20: the API returns the seven tokens with the values listed and provenance=provisional; no UI string or document claims official Mobily brand compliance

REQ-S15-003 USER DG6 M0300 | Validate contrast for every text/background token pair, derive an accessible action-button shade, and use separate semantic status tokens that always carry labels or icons, never using blue to imply a favourable status 
   PROC: An automated check computes WCAG contrast for every text/background combination and fails the build below 4.5:1 (3:1 for large text); status chips render a label and icon with the colour 
   ACC: A20: the contrast test lists every pair and passes; white small text on #0078FF is not used for action buttons; status chips are distinguishable in greyscale

REQ-DLV-002 ENGINEERING DG0 M0007;M0412 | Keep engineering delivery gates DG0-DG7 separate from product business approvals G1-G6 in records, authority and meaning 
   PROC: DG records live only under docs/delivery; G1-G6 are product records; project rules and every agent definition state that an engineering agent cannot grant a real business, Finance or IT approval 
   ACC: A23;A28: gate records validate only with stage_id DG0-DG7; CLAUDE.md and agent-protocol.md state that G6 never implies DG7 and that no agent grants a business, Finance or IT approval

REQ-DLV-041 ENGINEERING DG7 M0411;M0397 | Seal the DG7 release after approval: approve the frozen payload whose hash excludes review and gate metadata, append the DG7 gate record to the evidence envelope, run A28 integrity verification, and record the payload hash and archive checksum separately 
   PROC: After the DG7 audit the orchestrator builds the envelope, runs the A28 check and declares delivery complete only if sealing passes; a sealing failure blocks delivery and a payload change requires new candidate reviews 
   ACC: A28: the sealing check verifies that all eight gate records, the ten agent definitions, the register and the findings are present and match their checksums, that the payload hash equals the DG7 candidate ID, and that no DG record is confused with G1-G6

REQ-S12-009 USER DG4 M0229 | Starter automation: on a valid gate submission, route the exact evidence snapshot to the required approvers 
   PROC: Approval tasks reference the snapshot ID 
   ACC: A08;A13: each required approver receives exactly one task referencing the snapshot

REQ-PB-013 DG4 | Restrict Finance / Value Office validation of baseline, benefit logic and value realization to the Finance role 
    Only users holding FIN on the transformation can mark a baseline, benefit formula or realized value as validated; others can submit for validation 
    A10;A12: a Business Owner calling the validate endpoint receives 403; a Finance user succeeds and the audit event records validator identity

